## Goal
Flag a global function declared twice with the same name and parameter list within one plugin module, even when the two declarations live in different files.

## Source
tm-dips-plus-plus (2026-09-02). Vendored fallback sources: `src/Dependencies/Dep_SmPlayerVis.as` (generated from tm-sm-player-vis `src/Managers.as`) declares `uint16 GetOffset(const string &in, const string &in)`; `src/from-epp.as:47` declares the identical signature. Game compile failed; `openplanet-lsp check` on the full tree passed the gate with 0 errors (5 unrelated warnings).

## Repro
```angelscript
// FileA.as
uint16 GetOffset(const string &in className, const string &in memberName) { return 0; }

// FileB.as (same plugin)
uint16 GetOffset(const string &in className, const string &in memberName) { return 0xFFFF; }
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
from-epp.as (47, 1) :  ERR : A function with the same name and parameters already exists
Script compilation failed!
```
(The second declaration is the one blamed.)

## LSP today
Silent. Both files are compiled in the same module pass; no diagnostic is produced for either declaration.

## Acceptance
- [ ] Same name + same parameter list, two files, one plugin → error on the second declaration
- [ ] Same name + same parameter list within one file → error (same rule, likely same path)
- [ ] Same name with a genuinely different parameter list stays silent (legal overload)
- [ ] Same name in a different namespace stays silent
- [ ] Duplicate global *variables*/consts: verify the game rule and match it (not game-verified in this instance)
- [ ] Regression fixture

## Notes
Hit while vendoring byte-identical helper functions from two plugin repos into one host plugin (`Managers.as` in tm-char-vis and tm-sm-player-vis share `GetOffset`, `GetClassId`, `FindMgrIndex`, `GetManager`, `GetManagerPtr`). Any "bundle a copy of another plugin's sources" pattern will trip this class, and the LSP gate gives false confidence because the failure only surfaces in Openplanet.log.